    "result_text": "Changing the sheet's today now writes one `SNAPSHOT name=<name> due-total=<due-total>` line per person, and all 4 tests in `bin/e2e` pass.\n\nEach line shows the person's due-total on the day being left, or `n/a` when there isn't one. People are listed in the order they were added, which is the order the screen uses. The lines come before any period closes and before the change's ROLLUP/TOTALS lines.\n\nThe change is in two files:\n- **`Rollup.java`:** a new `recordSnapshot` method writes the lines. It uses the figures `setToday` already takes before the change, so no extra calculation is needed. Like the other audit lines, they are written only if the change saves, so a refused change writes nothing.\n- **`SheetService.setToday`:** it calls `recordSnapshot` first, but only when the new date is different from the current one.\n\nTwo choices the request didn't settle:\n- **Same date:** setting today to the date it already is writes no SNAPSHOT lines. I read \"changed\" as meaning the date actually changes.\n- **Acting for a steward:** when someone acting for a steward changes the date, the SNAPSHOT lines end with `for=<steward>`, like most audit lines. ROLLUP/TOTALS lines leave it off, so if SNAPSHOT should be treated as a figures-only line too, it's a one-line change in `Audit.java`. The test doesn't cover this case.",
